  "goodToKnow": "Die Rekonstruktion is reconstruction: of buildings, events or texts. Germany has debated many architectural Rekonstruktionen: Dresden's Frauenkirche (rebuilt 1994–2005), Berlin's Stadtschloss, reopened as the Humboldt Forum with reconstructed baroque façades, and Frankfurt's Neue Altstadt. Critics call them fake history; supporters see them as healing. Rekonstruieren means to reconstruct. Plural: die Rekonstruktionen."
